  "id": "Compound::DB00920 - Gene::5143",
  "verbalization": "Ketotifen is shown to bind to Pde7b and Pde8a, both of which are involved in the degradation of cyclic nucleotides, a key process in cellular signaling. These enzymes are functionally linked to the degradation of 3',5'-cyclic AMP, a second messenger that regulates various physiological processes. The evidence suggests that Ketotifen may inhibit Pde4c through a shared mechanism involving cyclic nucleotide degradation. The final scores from the three paths indicate a consistent and plausible relationship, with the most direct evidence coming from the binding to Pde7b and the subsequent involvement of Pde4c in cyclic nucleotide metabolism. The overlapping pathways and the presence of a common functional role in cyclic nucleotide degradation support the hypothesis that Ketotifen exerts its effects on Pde4c by modulating cyclic nucleotide levels. The integrated evidence suggests a mechanistic link between Ketotifen and Pde4c, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the specificity and potency of this interaction.",
